Z||000000||Simon Hudson||04-25-2001||02:07 AM||||Well, I’m finally a Fiero owner.  Though it’s not my dream car, at least it’s a start.  I picked up a 1986 Fiero SE from a buddy with only 132,000 km for $2500 Cdn.  IS there anything I should know that might prevent future problems and allow my new baby to run it’s best for as long as she’s able.  What particular maintenance should I do etc?  Thanks for your input.||||reg||10
Z||000001||khinden||04-25-2001||02:37 AM||||I, as well, am a Fiero owner.  I got an 85 SE 2.5l 4, 5-speed.  It isn't perfect, kinda rough.  The front and rear facias are from an 87-88 fiero.  the interior was alright but the passenger seat was trashed.  Luckly, I found an 86 se in a u-pull it junk yard.  I got both seats, hatch(trunk)carpet, rear passenger side vent, and other misc. interior parts.  I got it all for about 40 dollars.  I think I will go back and get to other parts.  The dash is still there, it is in good condition. I think I will get the front facia.  If anybody can think of something they need let me know.<BR>||||reg||1
